Other top nominees this year include Eladio Carrión, Farruko, Karol G, Manuel Turizo, Ovy on the Drums, Quevedo, Romeo Santos, Shakira, and Xavi, with six nominations each.&nbsp;

This year’s youth awards show will be held for the first time in Europe on Sept. 3 at the Starlite Auditorium in Marbella, Spain, following its past editions in Miami, Puerto Rico, and Panama.&nbsp;

This year’s ceremony, under the theme “Conéctate al Vibe” (“Connect to the Vibe”), will also coincide with the inauguration of PJ Fest, a weeklong event with creator activations and live concerts that will take place in Houston, Miami and Los Angeles, before culminating with the live gala in Spain.

The 2026 Premios Juventud—which celebrates the artists and young changemakers making an impact in music, social media and community service—will broadcast live on Sept. 3 via Univision, UNIMÁS, Galavisión, and ViX. Tickets to attend in person can be purchased here .

